/-- Rubric 4 (the starting slice is exhausted first). In any run, the first
`|X_b|` vertices all lie in the slice `X_b` of the initial vertex, `b = (p 0)_{n+1}`. [TraversingCombinatorial01Polytopes, node_05] -/
theorem starting_slice_exhausted {n : ℕ} (X : Finset (Fin (n + 1) → Bool))
    (p : ℕ → Fin (n + 1) → Bool) (hp : IsGreedyTraversal X p) :
    ∀ k, k < (X.filter (fun z => z (Fin.last n) = p 0 (Fin.last n))).card →
      p k (Fin.last n) = p 0 (Fin.last n) := by
  sorry

/-! ## Main theorem -/

/-- For every nonempty `X ⊆ {0,1}ⁿ`, every start and every tie resolution, the greedy
(λ, d)-lex traversal `x₁,…,x_N` is a Hamilton path in the skeleton of `conv(X)`. [TraversingCombinatorial01Polytopes, node_05] -/
